# Drop drivers/tools for hardware the BCM2710 boards do not have
# (openmanet_setup.sh ... -x bcm2710trim)
#
# Pi 3A+ / 3B+ / Zero 2 W: BCM2837, no PCIe bus at all, USB is a single DWC2
# (USB 2.0 OTG) controller, and there is no on-board ethernet PHY.
# All of the below are force-enabled as =y by boards/common/kmods_diffconfig or
# pulled in by common_extras/utils_diffconfig, i.e. inherited unconditionally.
#
# no PCIe bus -> lspci and its 1.4 MB id database are dead weight
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_pciutils is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_pciids is not set
#
# no xHCI silicon (Pi 4 gets USB3 from the VL805 xHCI *on PCIe*; BCM2837 has none)
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-usb3 is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-usb-xhci-hcd is not set
#
# DWC3 is the Synopsys USB *3.x* dual-role IP. No Pi has it (they use DWC2), yet
# kmod-usb-dwc3 carries AUTOLOAD so it is actually modprobed at boot.
# Only octeon / ipq40xx / ipq806x / qualcommax packages depend on it.
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-usb-dwc3 is not set
#
# device-tree MDIO, for an on-board ethernet PHY. Nothing on bcm2710 depends on
# it (only TARGET_bcm27xx_bcm2708 and friends do conditionally); on bcm2711 it
# was added to work around a lan78xx dependency bug - a Pi 4 concern.
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-of-mdio is not set
#
# KEPT ON PURPOSE (do not add):
#   kmod-libphy  - kmod-usb-net-asix-ax88179 DEPENDS on it, and AX88179 is the
#                  most common gigabit USB-RJ45 chipset. The bench dongle is the
#                  first-contact path on an eth-less 3A+; do not gamble on it.
#   usbutils/usbids - the board HAS USB; lsusb is needed to identify the dongle
#                  and the CM108 PTT adapter during bring-up.
#   tailscale    - user decision 2026-09-29: keep, may be needed later (upstream
#                  BLOS/RoIP path, enabled only on mesh gates by 16_openmanet_roip).
